# OpenClaw Workspace Conventions

## Required Files Per Workspace
Every `workspace-*/` directory should contain:
```
workspace-{agent}/
├── AGENTS.md       # Role definition, workflow, registry
├── SOUL.md         # Agent identity and behavioral directives  
├── USER.md         # User preferences and context (optional)
├── IDENTITY.md     # Agent self-model (optional)
├── BOOTSTRAP.md    # Startup instructions (optional)
├── TOOLS.md        # Available tools (optional)
├── HEARTBEAT.md    # Health/status tracking (optional)
└── .openclaw/
    └── workspace-state.json   # Runtime state
```

## Session Startup Order
1. Read `SOUL.md` — identity calibration
2. Read `USER.md` — user context
3. Read `memory/` daily files — recent context
4. Read `MEMORY.md` — persistent rules

## AGENTS.md Structure
```markdown
# AGENTS.md — {Role Name}

## System Role
[One sentence: what this agent does]

## Agent Registry
[Table of all agents in the system]

## Mandatory Workflow
[Pipeline definition]

## Task Classification
[Map task types to agents]
```

## SOUL.md Principles
- Terse. Direct. No corporate fluff.
- Define: primary directive, decision framework, boundaries
- Keep under 100 lines — identity, not documentation

## Memory Pattern
- `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` — daily session notes
- `MEMORY.md` — permanent rules and persistent context
- `sessions/*.jsonl` — full session history (auto-managed)
